    "turn_text": "now. Senator Talent, I think it's also a healthy exercise, at least for someone like me, to learn what would happen if America just what the didn't participate the way Trump was going, didn't try to bring Vladimir Putin to the table, didn't try to talk to Zelensky about what he's going to need to do to the concessions he's going to need. What is the alternative to the Donald Trump peace talks? How far does that go? Well, you see you put your finger on it. Again, you have to take into account what's happening happening on the battlefield in a war. We gave the Ukraine a chance to push Russia out of the territory. They had occupied. They started. We helped them start an offensive in the summer of 2023. It culminated in October of that year and it failed. The truth of the matter is neither side has been able to do maneuver warfare, Annie. That's agile warfare where you're able to concentrate all the elements of your force on the enemy's vulnerability. You can move quickly. You can get breakthroughs. They can't do it. So they've been fighting the alternative, which is attrition warfare. You wear the enemy down over time. In a battle like that, Russia has the advantage. They have more men to have more material, and that's before they bring in the North Koreans. They've just reduced the Kursk salient. Remember when Ukraine actually invaded a part of Russia and took some of it in Kursk province? The Russians have now eliminated that or all butt eliminated it. They're gradually forcing Ukrainians back, which I hate. But you know, it's like World War I with drones. That's what we're saying in Ukraine. So I don't think there is an alternative. And I'm concerned that if we wait and the situation gets worse, it's going to be even harder to get a decent deal. You know what the alternative is? Here's the alternative. The alternative is to tell Putin that if he doesn't come to a deal and give him the bottom line, that we're going to use American airpower and support of the Ukraine's. Eisenhower got a deal in Korea when he told the North Koreans, if you don't come to a settlement, I'm going to use nuclear weapons. Now, I don't know anybody who wants a direct confrontation between American forces and Russian forces, including the people who are the most hawkish right now and criticizing Trump from that perspective. Yeah. You know, they say this, we should give them a formal security guarantee. Well, first of all, we couldn't get Ukraine into NATO before the war. That requires unanimity. Europeans weren't going to do it. All these Europeans who say now they want to support Ukraine. And the second thing is, if you believe that we should give Ukraine a formal security guarantee against future invasions, then why aren't you suggesting that we fight for them now during this invasion? But I just think the people, and look, I'm open-minded to anything, and all I care about, I mean, basically, is American interests. I hate to sound bloodless because there have been over a million casualties,",
