    "turn_text": "you've said that you agree that if he were the president, it wouldn't have happened. He has to play the handies dealt now. He can't go back and undo what has been done. Certainly lives have been lost on both sides, almost immeasurable. Do you believe, like, what, what is it about? Donald Trump being the president when this minor incursion becomes a full blown war. What is it about Donald Trump being president then that disallows this from getting to the point where it is right now? That would have prevented it. Yeah. Because I think that, well, of course we don't, that's counterfactual history so we don't know for a certain. But what we do know is that after the disasters of Biden's first year, what he did in the first year was he rolled over a nuclear arms treaty called the new start treaty. He rolled it over, it was advantageous to Russia without conditions. So he gave the Russians that. He lifted the sanctions on the Nord Stream pipeline without conditions. He gave the Russians that. He gave Putin the summit. without conditions. And then we had the disastrous Afghanistan withdrawal. Now, do you think it's likely that communicated a message to Putin about the resolve and competency of American leadership and that that might have led him to believe he could just go in and take Ukraine and we wouldn't do anything and contrast that with Trump's leadership over four years. I just think we don't know for certain, but I think it's very plausible. that if they'd begun massing troops, the Trump who did not want to war in Eastern Europe would have let Russia know, I'm not going to tolerate this. So now he's got a difficult situation. As you say, he's entering at midstream, if you will. Now, there have been advantages to this. I strongly support it, the Ukrainian aid, and I still do. It has degraded the power of the Russian state. And since they made themselves an adversary to the United States and in the Middle East and in And in the Far East, they have t